            <ArticleTitle>[Clinical significance of the negative T wave and changes in the ST segment in the electrocardiogram of air force pilots].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>259-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>More and more investigators, consider that nonspecific ECG changes are significant in prognosis of appearance of ischemic heart disease. It is seldom, appearance of disorder in ECG records in so high selected population, as pilots in Air Force. Around 4% of flyers present ECG record which could be of clinical importance.</AbstractText>
